  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 130 AM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nA gradually weakening upper level ridge will continue the heat wave \nthrough the weekend.  Temperatures will remain 15 to 20 degrees \nabove normal today and Sunday with highs in the middle 90s to around \n100 degrees.  It will feel a little less stifling with dew points \ndipping down into the 60s and southwest to west winds increasing to \n5 to 10 mph.\n\nWith the upper ridge breaking down, models show a cold front pushing \ninto the PAH forecast area (fa) late Sunday into Sunday night. \nBehind the front, winds will shift to the north and 30-50% chances \nof showers and thunderstorms will spread into most of southern \nIllinois, southeast Missouri and southwest Indiana late Sunday night \ninto Monday morning. Chances will increase and spread southeast \nMonday afternoon across the entire PAH fa, with 60-70% chances north \nand west to 30-40% chances southeast. 30-40% chances will linger \nacross the entire area Monday night, tapering off west to east \nTuesday. Rainfall totals are not too impressive, generally from two \ntenths to a half inch. Dry conditions can then be expected the \nremainder of the work week. \n\nMore significant will be the return of cooler temperatures.  Highs \nMonday will range from the lower to middle 80s north to the lower \n90s south.  By Tuesday, highs will be near to actually a little \nbelow normal, ranging from the lower to middle 70s northwest to the \nlower 80s southeast. These highs will persist through the end \nof the week, with seasonable overnight lows in the middle 50s to\naround 60 degrees.",
